#### Removing the sex chromosome ###
First we need to check the assembly report on the NCBI Assembly page to see whether it is:
chromosome-level, scaffold-level, contig-level and whether X/Y chromosomes were identified.
The assembly report usually contains entries like: Chromosome X, Chromosome Y or only scaffolds. 
The reference genome that I have used is a chromsome level assembly and has entries like this: X	CM063105.1. Y chromosome is not annotated in this genome.

## removing the X chromosome from the vcf file ##

bcftools view \
    --targets ^CM063105.1 \
    variants_MinQ30_MinGQ30_SNPsOnly_PASS_mac3_hwe0.5_imiss_0.9_miss_60_mid95percentile.recode.vcf \
    -Oz -o variants_MinQ30_MinGQ30_SNPsOnly_PASS_mac3_hwe0.5_imiss_0.9_miss_60_mid95percentile_autosomes_only.vcf

